{"id": "successor-01.working.q.geometry", "status": "authority/scope and descriptive wording corrected", "original_check": "Decode assets/working.png as exactly 64x16: four horizontal 16x16 cells at x=0,16,32,48 with no gutters or added canvas between or around the cells (transparent margin inside a cell is composition, not padding). Consumer basis: src/queue-view-successor.ts declares running frames 4 (the sheet's cell count, unchanged under either preference), display.cell [16,16] and frameMs 100; the successor fixture draws only when width == 16*frames and height == 16, slices frame*16,0,16,16 and derives the frame from frameAt() (floor(elapsed/100) mod 4 when animating; the held cell otherwise).", "original_authority": "requirement", "original_scope": "whole Working sheet (both motion preferences)", "domain": "mechanical", "mode": "local", "carries": ["authoring-01.working.q.geometry"], "corrected_check": "Decode assets/working.png as exactly 64x16: four horizontal 16x16 cells at x=0,16,32,48 with no gutters or added canvas between or around the cells (transparent margin inside a cell is composition, not padding). Consumer basis (unchanged original module src/queue-view.ts lines 4 and 9; identical constants in the proposed successor module lines 8 and 13): running frames 4 (the sheet's cell count, unchanged under either preference), display.cell [16,16] and frameMs 100. Fixture behaviour, descriptive only and scoped to this successor destination as designed: the successor fixture draws only when width == 16*frames and height == 16, slices frame*16,0,16,16 and derives the frame from frameAt() (floor(elapsed/100) mod 4 when animating; the held cell otherwise).", "authority_label_for_record": "requirement (sheet geometry: owner + original consumer); fixture clause descriptive", "clauses": [{"text": "Decode assets/working.png as exactly 64x16: four horizontal 16x16 cells at x=0,16,32,48", "class": "owner", "scope": "whole sheet, both preferences"}, {"text": "with no gutters or added canvas between or around the cells (transparent margin inside a cell is composition, not padding)", "class": "fixture_fact", "scope": "whole sheet"}, {"text": "Consumer basis: src/queue-view-successor.ts declares running frames 4 ..., display.cell [16,16] and frameMs 100", "class": "consumer_fact_original", "scope": "whole sheet; the proposed module repeats the same constants"}, {"text": "the successor fixture draws only when width == 16*frames ..., slices frame*16,0,16,16 and derives the frame from frameAt() (floor(elapsed/100) mod 4 when animating; the held cell otherwise)", "class": "fixture_fact", "scope": "this successor destination as designed (src/queue-view-successor.ts + renderer-successor/); re-derive if the module changes"}], "expert_clauses": [], "evidence_route": null, "sources_added": [], "change_explanation": "C3/S7: the geometry obligation is attributed to the owner line and the unchanged original module so it does not depend on adopting the successor module; the fixture sentence is marked descriptive and scoped to the implementation. Outcome unchanged.", "maps_to": ["C3", "S7"]}
{"id": "successor-01.working.q.transparent-exterior-measured", "status": "authority split and wording corrected", "original_check": "MEASURED record (mechanical/local, diagnostic): retain every cell's alpha histogram and exact RGBA component boxes (zero-based, half-open). FLAG for visual review any alpha>0 component touching all four cell edges, or any single alpha>0 component covering more than half of the cell's 256 pixels. The flag is a diagnostic proxy for a canvas matte or grey tile and is NOT a rejection condition (a corner-to-corner X or full-span glyph legitimately touches all four edges with a transparent exterior). RGB values of alpha-0 pixels are not significant. Mechanical REJECTION is decidable only under the seed-rotation construction: each cell's alpha channel must equal that of cw^k(seed) under dst(x,y)=src(y,15-x) (224 alpha-0 and 32 alpha-255 pixels per cell). Outside that construction the measured record carries no rejection rule.", "original_authority": "observation", "original_scope": "diagnostic proxy for every cell; triggers visual review; not a rejection rule. Mechanical rejection form only under the seed-rotation construction.", "domain": "mechanical", "mode": "local", "carries": ["authoring-01.working.q.transparent-exterior"], "corrected_check": "MEASURED record (mechanical/local, diagnostic): retain every cell's alpha histogram and exact RGBA component boxes (zero-based, half-open). FLAG for visual review any alpha>0 component touching all four cell edges, or any single alpha>0 component covering more than half of the cell's 256 pixels. The flag is a diagnostic proxy for a canvas matte or grey tile and is NOT a rejection condition (a corner-to-corner X or full-span glyph legitimately touches all four edges with a transparent exterior). RGB values of alpha-0 pixels are not significant. PROPOSAL (seed-rotation construction only): mechanical REJECTION is decidable only under that construction, where each cell's alpha channel must equal that of cw^k(seed) under dst(x,y)=src(y,15-x) (for the current seed 21f5baca...: measured 224 alpha-0 / 32 alpha-255 pixels per cell). Outside that construction the measured record carries no rejection rule.", "authority_label_for_record": "observation (measurement and flag) + proposal (construction-scoped rejection clause)", "clauses": [{"text": "retain every cell's alpha histogram and exact RGBA component boxes (zero-based, half-open)", "class": "method", "scope": "every Working cell incl. the held cell"}, {"text": "FLAG for visual review any alpha>0 component touching all four cell edges, or ... more than half of the cell's 256 pixels ... NOT a rejection condition", "class": "diagnostic", "scope": "every Working cell incl. the held cell"}, {"text": "RGB values of alpha-0 pixels are not significant", "class": "non_restriction", "scope": "every Working cell incl. the held cell"}, {"text": "Mechanical REJECTION is decidable only under the seed-rotation construction: each cell's alpha channel must equal that of cw^k(seed) ... (224 alpha-0 and 32 alpha-255 pixels per cell)", "class": "expert_choice", "scope": "seed-rotation construction only (proposal)"}], "expert_clauses": [], "evidence_route": null, "sources_added": [], "change_explanation": "C6: the construction-scoped rejection clause is labelled proposal; S8: the 224/32 counts are stated as measured values of the current seed. Flag stays diagnostic; D1 split unchanged.", "maps_to": ["C6", "S8"]}
{"id": "successor-01.working.q.transparent-exterior-visual", "status": "unchanged", "original_check": "VISUAL record (visual/visual; the deciding rule): viewed at 1x and 3x on #172336, the exterior of every frame, including the held cell when stationary shows the panel with no unintended matte, tile, plate, halo or fringe; a deliberate opaque backing shape is acceptable only when it is part of the mark's recorded design and the exterior stays transparent. Partial alpha on mark pixels is permitted; binary alpha is not required. The rejected generated frame whose background held 193 opaque #808080 pixels is the failure class, not the definition of the rule.", "original_authority": "requirement", "original_scope": "whole Working sheet; deciding rule for the transparent-exterior outcome", "domain": "visual", "mode": "visual", "carries": ["authoring-01.working.q.transparent-exterior"], "corrected_check": "(unchanged)", "authority_label_for_record": "requirement", "clauses": [{"text": "the exterior ... shows the panel with no unintended matte, tile, plate, halo or fringe (including the held cell when stationary)", "class": "owner", "scope": "whole Working sheet"}, {"text": "a deliberate opaque backing shape is acceptable only when it is part of the mark's recorded design and the exterior stays transparent", "class": "inference", "scope": "whole Working sheet"}, {"text": "Partial alpha on mark pixels is permitted; binary alpha is not required", "class": "non_restriction", "scope": "whole Working sheet"}, {"text": "viewed at 1x and 3x on #172336", "class": "owner", "scope": "review conditions"}, {"text": "The rejected generated frame whose background held 193 opaque #808080 pixels is the failure class, not the definition of the rule", "class": "measured", "scope": "example"}], "expert_clauses": [], "evidence_route": "saved native/enlarged candidate views (fixture captures or pixl_inspection views); specialist views in specialist-views/ are preliminary, not the acceptance review", "sources_added": [], "change_explanation": "No change (caller keep).", "maps_to": []}
{"id": "successor-01.working.q.frame-assembly", "status": "sources/basis corrected (check unchanged)", "original_check": "For the successor the candidate sheet is the existing assets/working.png (sha256 cf101610...), already the exact 64x16 four-cell sheet, so no assembly step occurs and this clause is satisfied vacuously; the retained record must still name the exact candidate bytes and their provenance (byte-identical to accepted live.working-animation-motion-01.candidate; cells equal cw^k(seed) on alpha and visible RGBA). If a future provider result is not already the exact 64x16 four-cell sheet, the retained assembly record names the exact source frames or cell rectangles in play order and every delivered cell is a lossless copy: identical alpha everywhere and identical RGBA where alpha>0 (RGB of alpha-0 pixels is not significant); no resize, resample or recolor; no undocumented duplication or silent frame drop (a deliberately repeated phase is allowed when the record says so); all raw provider outputs are retained beside the assembled strip.", "original_authority": "requirement", "original_scope": "this successor branch; conditional on any new assembly; the reuse case records provenance only", "domain": "mechanical", "mode": "local", "carries": ["authoring-01.working.q.frame-assembly"], "corrected_check": "(unchanged)", "authority_label_for_record": "requirement (assignment process requirement, AUTHORING-STAGE.md 31-32) with a reuse-case provenance record; construction clause proposal", "clauses": [{"text": "For the successor the candidate sheet is the existing assets/working.png (sha256 cf101610...) ... no assembly step occurs and this clause is satisfied vacuously", "class": "measured", "scope": "reuse case"}, {"text": "the retained record must still name the exact candidate bytes and their provenance (byte-identical to accepted live.working-animation-motion-01.candidate; cells equal cw^k(seed) on alpha and visible RGBA)", "class": "expert_choice", "scope": "reuse case; provenance only"}, {"text": "If a future provider result is not already the exact 64x16 four-cell sheet, the retained assembly record names the exact source frames or cell rectangles in play order and every delivered cell is a lossless copy ...; all raw provider outputs are retained", "class": "assignment_process", "scope": "conditional on any new assembly"}, {"text": "(a deliberately repeated phase is allowed when the record says so) ... identical alpha everywhere and identical RGBA where alpha>0 (RGB of alpha-0 pixels is not significant)", "class": "non_restriction", "scope": "conditional"}], "expert_clauses": ["Under the seed-rotation construction, delivered cell k equals cw^k(seed) under dst(x,y)=src(y,15-x)."], "evidence_route": null, "sources_added": [{"id": "authoring-stage", "lines": [31, 32], "locator": "stage-assembly", "sha256": "29e73af9a110353dd1453b1bbbb73d7166cf42a0b8eb97f71b53e73701b600aa"}], "change_explanation": "C11/S3: the assembly-policy obligation is cited to AUTHORING-STAGE.md lines 31-32 (added to the source index); FOCUSED-SUCCESSOR lines 40-43 remain the reuse authorisation. Check text unchanged.", "maps_to": ["C11", "S3"]}
{"id": "successor-01.working.q.activity-not-success", "status": "check and scope corrected", "original_check": "Viewed at 1x and 3x nearest on #172336 (beside the exact Ready baseline as the comparison method), the running loop and each individual frame read as ongoing activity and not as completion: no frame forms a check mark or another success-like terminal pose.", "original_authority": "requirement", "original_scope": "loop: whole asset (requirement); per-frame: expert clause with rationale", "domain": "visual", "mode": "visual", "carries": ["authoring-01.working.q.activity-not-success"], "corrected_check": "Viewed at 1x and 3x nearest on #172336 (beside the exact Ready baseline as the comparison method). REQUIRED (owner, BRIEF line 3; PLAR 560-570 state_meaning): the running loop reads as ongoing activity and not as completion, with no completion/success silhouette or success-like terminal pose in the loop. REQUIRED (caller update, PLAR line 422; judged in stationary-meaning): the held cell, shown alone under reduced motion, reads as activity and not as completion. EXPERT CLAUSE (specialist; scope this successor): each transient frame (cells 1-3), seen singly, also reads as activity rather than completion, because frames are exposed singly for 100 ms and frame 0 is painted at cell creation.", "authority_label_for_record": "requirement (loop: owner; held cell: caller update) + proposal (transient frames singly)", "clauses": [{"text": "the running loop reads as ongoing activity and not as completion ... no completion/success silhouette or success-like terminal pose in the loop", "class": "owner", "scope": "whole asset"}, {"text": "the held cell, shown alone under reduced motion, reads as activity and not as completion", "class": "caller_update", "scope": "held cell (judged in stationary-meaning)"}, {"text": "each transient frame (cells 1-3), seen singly, also reads as activity rather than completion", "class": "expert_choice", "scope": "this successor; specialist clause with the 100 ms / painted-at-creation rationale"}, {"text": "beside the exact Ready baseline as the comparison method", "class": "method", "scope": "method"}, {"text": "Viewed at 1x and 3x nearest on #172336", "class": "owner", "scope": "review conditions"}], "expert_clauses": ["Avoid frames that read as the static symbol of another member (preserved Start arrowhead, paired pause bars)."], "evidence_route": null, "sources_added": [], "change_explanation": "C4/S4: the per-frame clause is split out of the owner requirement; loop and held cell remain required; transient frames become a scoped expert clause.", "maps_to": ["C4", "S4"]}
{"id": "successor-01.working.q.motion-continuity", "status": "evidence route named (check unchanged)", "original_check": "Under normal motion, play the actual four frames at the consumer's 100 ms per frame including the fourth-to-first wrap, at 1x and 3x on #172336. Required outcome: the strip plays as one continuous activity loop with no visible discontinuity at the fourth-to-first wrap. All four frames remain in the sheet and in play under normal motion; the reduced-motion hold does not remove or reorder them.", "original_authority": "requirement", "original_scope": "whole Working sheet under normal motion", "domain": "visual", "mode": "visual", "carries": ["authoring-01.working.q.motion-continuity"], "corrected_check": "(unchanged)", "authority_label_for_record": "requirement (one continuous loop at the consumer's 100 ms with no visible wrap discontinuity) + expert clauses (D2)", "clauses": [{"text": "play the actual four frames at the consumer's 100 ms per frame including the fourth-to-first wrap, at 1x and 3x on #172336", "class": "owner", "scope": "whole sheet under normal motion"}, {"text": "the strip plays as one continuous activity loop with no visible discontinuity at the fourth-to-first wrap", "class": "owner", "scope": "whole sheet under normal motion"}, {"text": "All four frames remain in the sheet and in play under normal motion; the reduced-motion hold does not remove or reorder them", "class": "caller_update", "scope": "both preferences"}, {"text": "[evidence route] saved views / actual playback", "class": "fixture_fact", "scope": "temporal evidence"}], "expert_clauses": ["Stable centre/anchor and stable visual volume across phases (both consumers paint into a fixed 16x16 cell; drift reads as jitter).", "Motion evenly paced across the four frames with no near-hold (a held pair at 4 x 100 ms reads as a stutter).", "Stable cluster count (three components per cell) and stepped quarter-turn phases with no morphing."], "evidence_route": "Three separate legs: (1) frameMs 100 constant in the consumer module = mechanical; (2) frame-index arithmetic on the synthetic capture timeline incl. the 400 ms wrap = mechanical (check.py 148-166); (3) actual playback = visual/temporal: caller viewing of the live fixture page under normal motion, available at 3x only in the current fixture; 1x playback requires a fixture change (a 1x live cell) or a separately labelled viewing aid; recorded as a visual observation, never as a checker pass. Wall-clock cadence is not measured and not claimed.", "sources_added": [], "change_explanation": "C10/S5 (narrowed): the actual-playback leg is routed to caller viewing of the live fixture page under normal motion, which exists only at 3x as the fixture stands (live cells at display.scale, view.mjs line 105; animate() repaints only liveCells, line 124; the 1x matrix is painted once at elapsed 0, lines 56 and 95). Check text unchanged.", "maps_to": ["C10", "S5"]}
